    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0472" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg460"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.00/1781: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-08"
                            >September 8, 1943</date>.<lb/>[Received September 9—3 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2071. Embassy’s No. 2063.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d415-f1"/> Final edition of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Noticias Gráficas</hi> confiscated and paper suspended
                    indefinitely for forthright editorial today. Tucuman newspaper <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La Unión</hi> closed for 2 days by federal interventor
                    for nature of headline comment especially one reading “sharp reply of Cordell
                    Hull: he makes charges.” Other provincial papers including <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La Voz del Interior</hi> of Córdoba and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">El Diario</hi> of Paraná are known to have been warned
                    not to comment on exchange of notes. Foregoing measures taken against press
                    despite assurances given by Chief of Press Office of the Presidency earlier
                    today that it was free to comment on this subject. It is also confirmed that
                    message was sent to all interventors by Ministry of the Interior advising them
                    that newspapers had been authorized to publish exchange of letters and to
                    comment thereon. Apparently, however, it was intended to be understood that the
                    comment be not critical.</p>
                <p>Publicity given this subject is overshadowed in evening papers by news of Italian
                    capitulation.</p>
                <pb facs="0473" n="461" xml:id="pg461"/>
                <p>Embassy’s No. 2061, September 8, 6 p.m.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d415-f2"/>
                    According to Argentine press source Storni told correspondents this evening that
                    in view of situation created by publication of exchange of correspondence and
                    fall of Italy there was now no possibility of severance of relations with Axis
                    countries. Rumors continue to circulate that Governmental changes are impending,
                    hastened by foregoing developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
